 trying to show y'all i'm just gonna  wipe that out real quick yummy  i will say the taste of the mozzarella  and the kimchi pokemop really go well  together  i also know some of you might be  confused as to why a video of a girl  saying cheese kim pop on a variety show  has the power to garner like millions  and millions of views uh and that would  go back to something that koreans call  egg yo  which is a quality of cuteness  that i feel like has the level of draw  or desirability that  maybe americans would consider hotness  or beauty  but anyways before we go today's twice  fact is that twice has actually been  featured in questions on school exams in  both taiwan  and korea so today's breakfast is  inspired by tahiana she  is a literal ray of sunshine and is one  of the rappers it's a vocalist for the  group  and she loves sweets particularly  chocolate and she says that one of her  favorite drinks is chocolate milk so  that's what i'm having for breakfast but  i couldn't just have chocolate milk so  i'm also having a little korean pastry  on the side  there's something so comforting about  chocolate milk that just reminds me of  childhood so good i know i've already  eaten noodles a lot this challenge but  apparently ramen is one of these staples  for the girls of twice  and they eat it a ton especially because  they're on the road often and it's super  quick easy and  obviously delicious i also chose ramen  for times lunch  specifically because there was an  interview where chaeyoung was asked  if taeyeon was a food what would she be  and she said  ramen which makes sense because taiyon  is so playful and bubbly  and i feel like everyone likes her just  like everyone likes ramen  so much sodium so satisfying also for  anyone who wants to get a sense of  tahan's  very outgoing personality you can see  that she actually went  viral prior to debuting with twice for a  dance that's known as the eagle dance  that she did as she was leading dance in  church  she was literally like so dinner tonight  is inspired by chaeyoung  she is a main rapper and sub vocalist  for the group she's also  extremely fashionable and really  artistic where she said that if you  weren't an idol right now she would have  actually tried to go to art school which  is really cool  she says that one of her favorite foods  is fruits and veggies we love a healthy  queen and i saw and i think what was a v  live her having this really delicious  looking arugula salad with tomatoes  so that's what i decided to have for  dinner tonight i'm really excited to eat  this because honestly i've eaten  very few vegetables this week so this is  very refreshing  anyways before i go today's twice fact  is that twice's debut video  like uh was their first to hit 100  million views on youtube  it hit the milestone in november 2016  after one year  and 23 days exactly so it is quite late  now but another aspect  of twice's routine that i thought i'd  try to replicate is their skin  care chaeyoung and nyon did a v live  showing their  nighttime getting unready routine i  personally really appreciated that they  would share this with their fans because  i feel like it's kind of rare to see  kpop idols  without perfect makeup on and it just  felt so casual and down to earth like  we're out of sleep over taking off our  makeup altogether  and you already know i was taking  furious notes to figure out how they get  that incredible glass skin  in the live nyan and chaeyoung used  three cleansers starting with a makeup  remover wipe  a foam cleanser and an oil cleanser to  get all that stage makeup off  chiang used some essence and then they  used a classic korean sheet mask which  nyon says she uses literally every day  and they ended it off with some lip balm  night cream and eye cream  i can't believe it is the last day of  our challenge but we're kicking off  today  with a chewy breakfast chewy is the  maknae of the group aka the youngest  member  she's also the only member from taiwan  she is an incredible vocalist and dancer  and has even inspired a skateboarding  mobile game which i sadly couldn't  download because they don't offer it for  iphone  she is known for loving bread and  pastries so of course i had to have  some bread in my breakfast additionally  i saw in a recent interview that on a  trip to thailand she really enjoyed this  drink called tang mopan it is a super  refreshing watermelon smoothie so that's  what i decided to pair my pastry with  it is so refreshing and light this  honestly reminds me of like a tropical  cocktail that you might get  but it's literally like 9 a.m right now  so obviously i'm having mine  alcohol free i'm already so hungry for  lunch and i'm really excited  making another favorite that chewie has  mentioned in an interview and that is  gonde namup which people sometimes call  korean thistle with rice it apparently  was commonly eaten in buddhist temples  it's supposed to be really good for you  i'm just having mine with a bunch of  veggies and panchon kimchi all that good  stuff  it's like a really yummy kind of earthy  flavor i know i often make a lot of meat  dishes  this is an excellent vegan option that i  would highly highly recommend  in addition to eating healthy most of  the time chaeyoung also says that she  really likes gummies i think a lot of  the girls in twice actually have said  that they like gummies  asian snacks are the best and my sister  here is a gummy fiend  so figured we would try some of these  different gummies we eat these all the  time  we love some fettuccine these are  another classic  individually wrapped pieces solid  i'm trying a little strawberry gummy  it's so cute  mango it really does taste like the  fruit i thought these looked really cute  also they're little peach gummies a  little booty peach it has good texture  i think the fettuccine is my favorite so  i think i have to agree  glad we got to try one of twice's guilty  pleasures if you want to partake in some  asian gummies as well  this stuff's really good it is our last  meal of eating like twice so i thought  it ended off with a meal that i know all  the girls  enjoy together and that is chapchae  which is just stir-fried sweet potato  noodles with veggies and normally some  beef i made mine vegetarian though and  goguma matang which is candied sweet  potato i  unfortunately made the rookie mistake of  buying american sweet potatoes instead  of the korean goguma sweet potato  which is white rather than orange but  when you're frying and candying a sweet  potato i feel like it tastes good either  way in a recent interview i watched  twice was talking about how they often  would order food together and eat  together which makes sense because  they're constantly traveling  training on the road and i think it's  really sweet that they share so many  meals honestly it's like having  a second family because they spend so  much of their time together  so obviously i'm starting out with the  chapter which is the savory dish that i  made  seasoning with the soy sauce and sugar  is so  easy so definitely an a1 dish if you're  new to cooking it's kind of hard to mess  up and of course before we move on to  dessert have to finish off with my final  twice fact and that is that the official  fandom name  once was announced on november 4th 2015  through their official instagram account  the group said if you love us even once  we will repay your love with twice our  love we will work hard so you can look  at us once  and fall in love with twice let's be  together until the end  gotta finish off the video with some  dessert  that crunch the crystallization is so  good  and honestly y'all as i'm looking back  on this week we made  so many delicious meals but i have to  say i think if you're going to make  one dish from this week i would  recommend momo's  choc par just the complexity of the  seasonings are so delicious  and if you're vegan or vegetarian i  definitely would recommend just trying  that little marinade with all the  seasonings  and rather than raising pig's feet  definitely some potatoes some veggies  all that good stuff would taste  delicious in it over some rice i had so  much fun recreating all of these twice  foods this week i hope you learned a  little bit more about twice as well as  about korean culture and if there's  anyone you'd like me to eat like next  let me know in the comments down below  and i'll see you in the next one bye  [Music]  you
 

